       one of the signals specified in the signal  set  _s_e_t  becomes  pending.
       For  a signal to become pending, it must first be blocked with ssiiggpprroocc‐‐
       mmaasskk(2).  The function accepts the signal (removes it from the  pending
       list of signals), and returns the signal number in _s_i_g.

       The operation of ssiiggwwaaiitt() is the same as ssiiggwwaaiittiinnffoo(2), except that:

       •  ssiiggwwaaiitt()  returns  only  the signal number, rather than a _s_i_g_i_n_f_o___t
          structure describing the signal.

       •  The return values of the two functions are different.

